<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I875fbf4b78f5a5903227b349b2cc2f5811a4b689" commit="45044127bc108fda32a83e640201233fe0557b94" commit_message="FAFT: Check for EC flash access before changing WP  Do not attempt to change the write-protect setting on the EC flash region if this region is inaccessible to the AP. This means that devices with this property in their FAFT configuration will skip tests that need to change the WP setting as N/A.  BUG=b:126735368 TEST=Ran firmware_ECWriteProtect, firmware_ECSoftwareSync, firmware_ECUpdateId on Arcada  Change-Id: I875fbf4b78f5a5903227b349b2cc2f5811a4b689 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1496155 Commit-Ready: Abe Levkoy &lt;alevkoy@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Abe Levkoy &lt;alevkoy@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="1496155" owner_email="alevkoy@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/55/1496155/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I1a9818a9e690cd518a258be428a4f10cfa0f0125" commit="e9f632a1502d008fac12686d759fd7a6ad93fbdd" commit_message="FAFT: Check for Chrome EC before trying to use it  Several FAFT tests perform operations on the Chrome EC by accessing FirmwareTest.ec. This attribute only exists, and these operations only make sense, on devices that actually have a Chrome EC. Skip these tests as N/A on other devices.  BUG=b:125837981 TEST=Ran modified tests on Arcada  Change-Id: I1a9818a9e690cd518a258be428a4f10cfa0f0125 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1496156 Commit-Ready: Abe Levkoy &lt;alevkoy@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Abe Levkoy &lt;alevkoy@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Raul E Rangel &lt;rrangel@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="1496156" owner_email="alevkoy@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/56/1496156/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2d76546eb26edbbe2394cbca968cacb64365d910" commit="9ebb767169ff6eeb4697e6349fdb55002d7d5970" commit_message="FAFT: Check for Chrome EC in Cr50 tests  firmware_Cr50DeviceState and firmware_Cr50ECReset rely on the Chrome EC to exercise the EC. In these tests, check whether the DUT has a Chrome EC before trying to use it.  BUG=b:125837981 TEST=Ran tests on Arcada  Change-Id: I2d76546eb26edbbe2394cbca968cacb64365d910 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1506620 Commit-Ready: Abe Levkoy &lt;alevkoy@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Abe Levkoy &lt;alevkoy@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Raul E Rangel &lt;rrangel@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="1506620" owner_email="alevkoy@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/20/1506620/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ib4abbf63c4997362e1ae5a4be961e412b0dc5192" commit="dd91abfb01a5e8f03dee1beebc40bd8d257c7e40" commit_message="vboot: Adjust to VbExDisplayDebugInfo() API change  A parameter was added to this API, use it.  CQ-DEPEND=CL:1497038 BRANCH=None BUG=None TEST=compiles  Change-Id: Ib4abbf63c4997362e1ae5a4be961e412b0dc5192 Signed-off-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1496903 Reviewed-by: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="1496903" owner_email="jwerner@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" ref="refs/changes/03/1496903/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I52a1e764189508130fea562ad6d53bcefb1fce64" commit="60071a3f21eb94e9471a3d2ad1651657462bc504" commit_message="vboot_display: Add full_info parameter to VbExDisplayDebugInfo()  VbExDisplayDebugInfo() was invented for the TAB display that dumps a whole lot of possibly interesting debug data to the screen. Since some debug data is only available to the calling firmware, the convention has always been that the calling firmware is supposed to append any of its own debug data it thinks may be relevant to the output.  Later, the function was reused to print small info messages that give the user a hint what went wrong when a Ctrl+U or Ctrl+L fails (unlocalized, of course, but better than nothing). The calling firmware is not aware of this new use case, so every time vboot prints a &quot;WARNING: Ctrl+L not enabled&quot; sort of message on the screen, depthcharge also dumps the firmware IDs and TPM state below it.  This patch introduces a new parameter to the function to make the two differing use cases clear to the calling firmware.  CQ-DEPEND=CL:1496903 BRANCH=None BUG=None TEST=with other patches  Change-Id: I52a1e764189508130fea562ad6d53bcefb1fce64 Signed-off-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1497038 " fail_count="3" gerrit_number="1497038" owner_email="jwerner@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" ref="refs/changes/38/1497038/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ic4257548bfa045e34860a4b4193492a343572ca1" commit="4c2bb2eeda510fdaa5ed04a02b30b77598f03196" commit_message="vboot/screens: Add handling for unprintable character to draw_text()  This patch enhances draw_text() to better handle unavailable (e.g. unprintable) characters (by drawing a '?' rather than stopping with the whole string right then and there). Pull the width measurement into get_char_image_filename() since all callers need to do that anyway, and also change the signature so that the function is no longer expected to sprintf() into a string buffer it doesn't know the length of.  BRANCH=None BUG=None TEST=with other patches  Change-Id: Ic4257548bfa045e34860a4b4193492a343572ca1 Signed-off-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1496904 Reviewed-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mathew King &lt;mathewk@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="1496904" owner_email="jwerner@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" ref="refs/changes/04/1496904/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-5.44" change_id="Ic37ffbcc15ecb0f7b63f8f990315761b1005b0da" commit="6c19ecc768b6495ceee549eb1602bbce4515476b" commit_message="bluetooth: replace suspend logic in powerd_suspend script with one in BlueZ  This changed enables logic that is already submitted however disabled in the code until all kernels support the change.  CL:1464385 introduced a new way to handle the Bluetooth events mask during suspend and resume. Up to now the that logic was disabled until all kernel versions support the new management 'set event mask' opcode. The new logic is based in BlueZ's interaction with powerd callbacks upon suspend and resume.  Enabling is done in two CLs: [This CL] Removing a temporary flag in BlueZ to disable Set Event Mask command [CL:1493216] Removing BT 'set event mask' done in powerd_suspend script  BUG=b:119700112 TEST=suspend and resume of 